    "report": "The contact details came back as `[hidden]` after a cancellation because the paid-stay check ignored paid bookings that had since been cancelled. That's fixed and committed on `main` (`871aa1e`); I did not push.\n\n**Cause:** `hasPaidStay` in `src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts` had an extra filter, `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'`. Once the traveller cancelled the paid booking, the query found nothing, and `GetConversationQueryHandler` masked the host's contact details again. The port's doc comment and the rule both say a paid stay counts even if later cancelled or refunded, so the filter contradicted them.\n\n**Fix:** I removed that filter. Nothing else in the query or the conversation view changed.\n\n**Test:** I extended the existing \"Contact details held back\" e2e test in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`. It now cancels the paid booking and checks the host's email still shows in full. The test fails without the fix and passes with it. The conversations e2e file and all Booking-matching e2e suites pass (140 suites, 813 tests), and Prettier is clean.\n\n**Choices and unclear points:**\n- The request didn't say whether a cancelled booking that was never paid should count. I left that case alone, since the query still requires a `paid` or `declared` payment.\n- You asked me to commit on the current branch, which is `main`, so the commit went there rather than to a feature branch.\n- I didn't run `yarn check:conventions` or `yarn lint`. The change is a one-line SQL edit plus a test, so I don't expect either to be affected.",
